            "observations": [
                "QWidget::grab() and QWidget::render() must be called on the GUI thread. Both are implemented by repainting the widget through QWidget::render(), so the call is synchronous and blocks the GUI thread for its duration.",
                "Neither call needs a current OpenGL context for raster widgets. A QWidget hierarchy that contains a QOpenGLWidget/D3D child is the case that needs a graphics context (see the openglwidget sample).",
                "Popups, QMenu and non-modal QDialog are separate top-level windows and are NOT part of a top-level widget capture. The target adapter must decide whether to share only the main window or to compose extra windows.",
                "Damage can be observed with public APIs by installing an application-level event filter and reading QPaintEvent::region(). Capture itself emits paint events, so capture-induced damage has to be separated from application damage.",
                "Reused target buffer: 169 reallocations were observed in 170 capture attempts. QImage is copy-on-write, so publishing a shallow copy to a consumer forces the producer's next write to detach and allocate a new buffer. Handing out a QImage therefore does not give a free buffer recycling scheme, and it is also why a consumer that keeps a QImage copy never observes torn pixels.",
                "Damage probe: application repaints covered 69.8 % of the frame area on average, while the capture calls themselves added 79.7 %; a region-based damage stream is available but capture-induced repaints are part of it."
